+# Feature Specification: Cancel Booking
+
+**Created**: 2026-11-17 | **Status**: Draft
+
+**Input**: Plans change, and customers ask us to cancel their bookings. `cancel(bookingId, at)` on the rental service cancels the booking at time `at` and returns `{ bookingId, refund }`, the amount given back to the customer. A cancelled booking no longer holds its equipment, and a booking can only be cancelled once.
+
+## User Scenarios & Testing
+
+### User Story 1 - Cancel a booking and refund the customer (P1)
+**Acceptance**:
+1. Given a 4-day booking with total 10000 starting at day D, when cancelled at or before D 00:00, then refund is 10000.
+2. Given the same booking, when cancelled after its start but before its end, then refund is for the unused whole hours only: `floor(total * remainingHours / totalHours)` (e.g. 1 day in: 7500).
+3. Given the same booking, when cancelled at or after its end, then refund is 0.
+4. Cancelling returns `{ bookingId, refund }`.
+
+### User Story 2 - Cancelled bookings free the equipment (P1)
+1. After cancellation, `book` for the same item and an overlapping period succeeds and `availability` lists the item.
+2. A second `cancel` of the same booking is refused with an error.
+3. Cancelling an unknown booking id is refused with an error.
+
+## Requirements
+- **FR-001**: `cancel(bookingId, at)` returns `{ bookingId, refund }`; refund is an integer number of cents.
+- **FR-002**: `at` must be an ISO-8601 UTC string on the hour, otherwise it throws and the booking stays active.
+- **FR-003**: Refund = total if `at <= start`; `floor(total * (end - at) / (end - start))` (measured in whole hours) if `start < at < end`; 0 if `at >= end`.
+- **FR-004**: A cancelled booking no longer blocks `book` or `availability`.
+- **FR-005**: Cancelling an unknown or already-cancelled booking throws; a failed cancel changes nothing.
+
+## Assumptions
+- The refund policy was not specified by the requester (unavailable for clarification); the prorated policy above was chosen as the most reasonable because it needs no invented thresholds and is derived from the booking itself.
+- `at` may lie outside the booking's period; it is never restricted to "now".
+- Refund is rounded down to whole cents, so the school never refunds more than the prorated amount.
+- Long-stay discount is already in the booking total; the refund is a share of that total.
+
+## Success Criteria
+- All acceptance scenarios pass as automated tests; existing tests remain valid.
